-- Broadcasting Act (Chapter 28): THE FIRST AND THIRD SCHEDULES, VERSION BY VERSION, ON TWO DATES.
-- A version of a Schedule has two dates: the day it takes effect (valid time) and the day it was published (rule-version time). A question has two days: the day of the conduct and the day the law is read as at.
-- The version read is the latest published on or before the reading day among those that take effect on or before the day of the conduct; where none qualifies the answer is NOTHING.
-- On an `unstable` build the same table would be read with the built-ins (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` or `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` for the conduct day, the rule-version axis `tcRuleVersionTime` for the reading day, system time for "today");
-- build 98 of `main` rejects them, so both days are inputs and the versions are data.
-- The versions are the texts deposited: the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003) and the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012), both from the e-Gazette; S 549/2012 and S 559/2010 (e-Gazette);
-- and the consolidation in force from 25 September 2024 (Singapore Statutes Online rendering). No text before 31 July 2003 was obtained, so a conduct day or a reading day before it answers NOTHING.
-- A reading day after `the day the sources were last checked` (4 November 2026, assumed, not ruled; see sgba-vintage.l4) also answers NOTHING: nothing is known of later versions.
-- A reading day from 2 October 2026 to that day is answered from the latest version deposited.
-- Sections 2(1) ("broadcasting apparatus"), 20(1) to (4), 47, 51, 57 and 60 read the same in the three editions (compared by script on 2026-11-03; the differences are drafting style: "no person shall" and "a person must not", spacing); the one difference of substance is s 57(3), which the 2003 and 2012 editions have and the 2024 text does not (deleted by Act 22 of 2016 s 93(h) from 1 October 2016, read on two days in `sgba-versions-later.l4`); NOTES.md records the comparison.
-- Whether a retrospective notification (S 549/2012 is "deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011") is valid, and what a court would do with conduct already past, is NOT addressed here:
-- the table takes the notification's deeming as the text states it.

§ `The First Schedule, version by version`

-- src:BA1994.20030731:2134 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2135 | Section 2 (1)
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2137 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2139 | 1. Broadcast television receiver.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2141 | 2. Broadcast sound receiver.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2143 | 3. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2145 | For the purposes of this Schedule —
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2146 | ‘‘broadcast sound receiver’’ means any apparatus used for the aural
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2147 | reception of any broadcasting service;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2148 | ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’ means any apparatus used for the visual and
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2149 | aural reception in monochrome or colour of any broadcasting service;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2150 | ‘‘television receive-only satellite receiving system’’ means any apparatus
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2151 | (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2152 | direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2153 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2154 | space.
@ref First Schedule, Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003) (src:BA1994.20030731:2134-2154)
`the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` MEANS
    `First Schedule version` WITH `source` IS "Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003), e-Gazette"
                                 , `takes effect on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                 , `published on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                 , `lists broadcast television receivers` IS TRUE
                                 , `lists broadcast sound receivers` IS TRUE
                                 , `lists TVRO systems` IS TRUE

