-- The table. Each row has an `@ref` and quotation lines above; the version made by S 549/2012 is in `sgba-i-s549-2012.l4`, with its own.
`the First Schedule versions` MEANS
    LIST `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`
       , `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2012`
       , `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012`
       , `the First Schedule in the consolidation in force from 25 September 2024`

GIVEN x IS A `First Schedule version`
      y IS A MAYBE `First Schedule version`
GIVETH A MAYBE `First Schedule version`
`the later published of two First Schedule versions` MEANS
    CONSIDER y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN JUST z THEN IF x's `published on` AT LEAST z's `published on` THEN JUST x ELSE JUST z

-- "Today": a reading day up to and including `the day the sources were last checked` (4 November 2026; assumed, not ruled, one line in sgba-vintage.l4) is answered from the latest version deposited.
-- The caveat that goes with every such answer: on 4 November 2026 the orchestrating session searched the e-Gazette index (first page of each of two searches) and read the three results that name the Act; none amends a provision of the Broadcasting Act (detail in sgba-vintage.l4). That is what a first-page index search and three readings show; it is not a finding that nothing exists. A later reading day answers NOTHING.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `First Schedule version`
`the First Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    IF reading AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`
    THEN foldr `the later published of two First Schedule versions` NOTHING (filter (GIVEN v YIELD v's `published on` AT MOST reading AND v's `takes effect on` AT MOST conduct) `the First Schedule versions`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN v IS A `First Schedule version`
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the equipment is an item of the First Schedule version` MEANS
    (v's `lists broadcast television receivers` AND e's `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour`) OR (v's `lists broadcast sound receivers` AND e's `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`) OR (v's `lists TVRO systems` AND e's `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite`)

§ `Section 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus", on two dates`

-- src:BA1994.20030731:198 | ‘‘broadcasting apparatus’’ means any apparatus capable of or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:199 | designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting
-- src:BA1994.20030731:200 | service and specified in the First Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus", Revised Edition 2003 (src:BA1994.20030731:198-200)
-- src:BA1994.20120831:191 | “broadcasting apparatus” means any apparatus capable of or
-- src:BA1994.20120831:192 | designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting
-- src:BA1994.20120831:193 | service and specified in the First Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus", Revised Edition 2012 (src:BA1994.20120831:191-193)
-- src:277 | “broadcasting apparatus” means any apparatus capable of or
-- src:278 | designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting
-- src:279 | service and specified in the First Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus", consolidation in force from 25 September 2024 (src:277-279)
-- Reading A (fork F-BA-01), the one the rest of the encoding takes: "specified in the First Schedule" qualifies the whole of "capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting service".
GIVEN v IS A `First Schedule version`
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading A` MEANS
    (e's `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` OR e's `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`) AND `the equipment is an item of the First Schedule version` v e

-- Reading B (fork F-BA-01): "specified in the First Schedule" qualifies only "designed or constructed for", so equipment capable of reception is broadcasting apparatus whether or not it is listed.
GIVEN v IS A `First Schedule version`
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading B` MEANS
    e's `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` OR (e's `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` AND `the equipment is an item of the First Schedule version` v e)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the First Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading A` v e)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the First Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading B` v e)

§ `Section 20(1), on two dates`

-- src:BA1994.20030731:701 | 20.—(1) Subject to this section, no person shall —
-- src:BA1994.20030731:702 | (a) install any broadcasting apparatus in any place, or on board
-- src:BA1994.20030731:703 | any ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:704 | (b) import, offer for sale, sell or have in his possession with a
-- src:BA1994.20030731:705 | view to sale, any broadcasting apparatus; or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:706 | (c) operate or have on any premises in Singapore owned or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:707 | occupied by him broadcasting apparatus on or by which
-- src:BA1994.20030731:708 | broadcasting services are received,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:709 | except under and in accordance with a licence granted under this
-- src:BA1994.20030731:710 | section.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:711 | (2) Every licence granted under subsection (1) shall be in such
-- src:BA1994.20030731:712 | form and for such period and may contain such terms and conditions
-- src:BA1994.20030731:713 | as the Authority may determine.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:714 | (3) Subsection (1) shall not be construed as requiring any person
-- src:BA1994.20030731:715 | who works a broadcasting apparatus in the course of his duty as a
-- src:BA1994.20030731:716 | member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Singapore Police Force,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:717 | the Vigilante Corps or the Singapore Civil Defence Force to obtain a
-- src:BA1994.20030731:718 | licence under this Act.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:719 | (4) The Authority may exempt any person or broadcasting
-- src:BA1994.20030731:720 | apparatus or class of broadcasting apparatus from subsection (1).
@ref s 20(1) to (4), Revised Edition 2003 (src:BA1994.20030731:701-720)
