-- The three editions read the same on these subsections (compared by script, 2026-11-03). A person is outside the subsection if licensed (and within the licence), or exempt under (3) or (4),
-- or, by section 60, exempted by a Ministerial order (asked as facts, as in sgba-p5-apparatus.l4).
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
      w IS A `Dealing with apparatus`
      `the dealing is under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, the apparatus or the class of apparatus is exempt under section 20(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` conduct reading e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST isBroadcastingApparatus THEN
        JUST (isBroadcastingApparatus AND (w's `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` OR w's `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` OR ((w's `operates it` OR w's `has it`) AND w's `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` AND w's `broadcasting services are received on or by it`)) AND (NOT `the dealing is under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`) AND (NOT `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)`) AND (NOT `the person, the apparatus or the class of apparatus is exempt under section 20(4)`) AND (NOT `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)`))

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      e IS A `Receiving equipment`
      w IS A `Dealing with apparatus`
      `the dealing is under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, the apparatus or the class of apparatus is exempt under section 20(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B` conduct reading e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST isBroadcastingApparatus THEN
        JUST (isBroadcastingApparatus AND (w's `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` OR w's `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` OR ((w's `operates it` OR w's `has it`) AND w's `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` AND w's `broadcasting services are received on or by it`)) AND (NOT `the dealing is under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`) AND (NOT `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)`) AND (NOT `the person, the apparatus or the class of apparatus is exempt under section 20(4)`) AND (NOT `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)`))

-- Reading B of F-BA-03 (NOTES.md): the premises phrase in paragraph (c) qualifies only "have", so "operate" is not confined to the person's own premises.
-- Reading A of F-BA-03 is the default in the functions above; the two functions below take reading B of F-BA-03 together with reading A, and with reading B, of F-BA-01.
