    CONSIDER y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN JUST z THEN IF x's `published on` AT LEAST z's `published on` THEN JUST x ELSE JUST z

-- "Today": a reading day up to and including `the day the sources were last checked` (4 November 2026; assumed, not ruled, one line in sgba-vintage.l4) is answered from the latest version deposited.
-- The caveat that goes with every such answer: on 4 November 2026 the orchestrating session searched the e-Gazette index (first page of each of two searches) and read the three results that name the Act; none amends a provision of the Broadcasting Act (detail in sgba-vintage.l4). That is what a first-page index search and three readings show; it is not a finding that nothing exists. A later reading day answers NOTHING.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Third Schedule version`
`the Third Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    IF reading AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`
    THEN foldr `the later published of two Third Schedule versions` NOTHING (filter (GIVEN v YIELD v's `published on` AT MOST reading AND v's `takes effect on` AT MOST conduct) `the Third Schedule versions`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1802 | “relevant licensable broadcasting service” means a licensable
-- src:1803 | broadcasting service specified in the first column of the
-- src:1804 | Third Schedule provided by a person specified in the second
-- src:1805 | column of that Schedule opposite the licensable broadcasting
-- src:1806 | service.
@ref s 31(6) "relevant licensable broadcasting service" (the Third Schedule's first and second columns), consolidation in force from 25 September 2024 (src:1802-1806)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `it is a subscription nationwide television service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider's name, as the Schedule prints it` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(6) the licensable broadcasting service is a relevant licensable broadcasting service, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`it is a subscription nationwide television service` AND elem `the provider's name, as the Schedule prints it` (v's `providers of the subscription nationwide television service`))

§ `The Television and Radio Licensing Regulations (Rg 1), version by version`

-- Three versions, each with two dates (see sgba-nouns.l4, `Rg 1 version`): the Revised Edition 2004 (29 February 2004, taken as published the same day), the Regulations as amended by S 333/2004 (in operation 21 June 2004, published 15 June 2004),
-- and the revocation by S 548/2012 (deemed in operation 1 January 2011, published 31 October 2012). The rows live in the instrument modules that quote them; the table and the selection are here.
-- The version read is the latest published on or before the reading day among those that take effect on or before the day of the conduct; none qualifying answers NOTHING.
-- No text of Rg 1 before 29 February 2004 was obtained, so a conduct day before that day answers NOTHING; so does a reading day before it. The savings of S 548/2012 reg 2(2) and the refund of reg 2(3) are rules in `sgba-i-s548-2012.l4`;
-- for the pairs of days the table covers they agree with the table (a matter before 1 January 2011 is read under the version that was in force then).
`the Rg 1 versions` MEANS
    LIST `Rg 1 as printed in the Revised Edition 2004`
       , `Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004`
       , `Rg 1 as revoked by S 548/2012`

GIVEN x IS A `Rg 1 version`
      y IS A MAYBE `Rg 1 version`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Rg 1 version`
`the later published of two Rg 1 versions` MEANS
    CONSIDER y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN JUST z THEN IF x's `published on` AT LEAST z's `published on` THEN JUST x ELSE JUST z

-- "Today": a reading day up to and including `the day the sources were last checked` (4 November 2026; assumed, not ruled, one line in sgba-vintage.l4) is answered from the latest version deposited.
-- The caveat that goes with every such answer: on 4 November 2026 the orchestrating session searched the e-Gazette index (first page of each of two searches) and read the three results that name the Act; none amends a provision of the Broadcasting Act (detail in sgba-vintage.l4); the search terms named the Act, not the Regulations. That is what a first-page index search and three readings show; it is not a finding that nothing exists. A later reading day answers NOTHING.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Rg 1 version`
`the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    IF reading AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`
    THEN foldr `the later published of two Rg 1 versions` NOTHING (filter (GIVEN v YIELD v's `published on` AT MOST reading AND v's `takes effect on` AT MOST conduct) `the Rg 1 versions`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- What each version of Rg 1 says about a licence for receiving equipment, one helper per regulation that S 333/2004 changed or added. A revoked Regulation says nothing: its answer is FALSE.
GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver, under the version` MEANS
    BRANCH IF v's `the text read` EQUALS "RevEd 2004" THEN `Rg 1 reg 23(1) a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver (RevEd 2004)` `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` `the receiver is in a vessel` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`
           IF v's `the text read` EQUALS "amended by S 333/2004" THEN `Rg 1 reg 23(2) a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver (S 333/2004)` `the receiver is in a vessel` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, under the version` MEANS
    IF v's `the text read` EQUALS "RevEd 2004"
    THEN `Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the regulation (RevEd 2004)` `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` `the person has a licence`
    ELSE FALSE

GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` MEANS
    IF v's `the Regulations are in force`
    THEN `Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver (RevEd 2004)` `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` `the receiver is in a vessel` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`
    ELSE FALSE

GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the receiver is installed in a commercial property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 29A(1) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` MEANS
    IF v's `the text read` EQUALS "amended by S 333/2004"
    THEN `Rg 1 reg 29A(1) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver (S 333/2004)` `the receiver is installed in a commercial property`
    ELSE FALSE

GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 24 and 29 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a receiver, under the version` MEANS
    IF v's `the Regulations are in force`
    THEN `Rg 1 reg 24 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a broadcast sound receiver` `the use is temporary` `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`
    ELSE FALSE

-- The dispatchers: the helper under the version read for the pair of days. NOTHING where no version qualifies.
-- Each dispatcher says what Rg 1 STATES IN TERMS in the version read, and its name says so: FALSE means that regulation says nothing of the kind, not that no licence was needed. A sound receiver that is not in a vehicle or a vessel, for instance, answers FALSE to the reg 23 dispatcher (which names a vehicle or a vessel), while whether s 20(1)(c) of the Act, stated above, requires a licence for it is a separate question (F-BA-12).
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for a broadcast sound receiver installed in a vehicle or in a vessel, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver, under the version` v `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` `the receiver is in a vessel` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 the person contravenes the prohibition on operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, under the version` v `the person operates a broadcast television receiver` `the person has a licence`)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(2) states in terms that a separate licence is required for a broadcast television receiver installed in a vehicle or vessel, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` v `the receiver is installed in a vehicle` `the receiver is in a vessel` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the receiver is installed in a commercial property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 29A(1) states in terms that a separate licence is required for a broadcast television receiver installed in a commercial property, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`Rg 1 reg 29A(1) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` v `the receiver is installed in a commercial property`)

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 regs 24 and 29 state in terms that a licence is not required for the temporary use of a receiver, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`Rg 1 reg 24 and 29 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a receiver, under the version` v `the use is temporary` `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`)

§ `The TVRO System Regulations, regulation 3(2), from 1 August 2001`

-- The institution-only rule is printed whole in S 354/2001 (in operation 1 August 2001) and in the Revised Edition 2004 (29 February 2004) in the same words. For conduct from 1 August 2001 to 28 February 2004 the S 354/2001 text answers;
-- from 29 February 2004 to the day the sources were last checked (4 November 2026, assumed, not ruled) the Revised Edition's text answers (as `sgba-i-tvro-regs.l4` does); before 1 August 2001 the text of reg 3 was not obtained (the original, G.N. S 126/1991, is not deposited), so the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`TVRO reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence, from 1 August 2001, for conduct on a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF conduct AT LEAST (Date 29 2 2004) THEN `reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence, on` conduct (`reg 2 the person is an institution` `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` `it is an undertaking`)
           IF conduct AT LEAST (Date 1 8 2001) THEN JUST (`S 354/2001 reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence` `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` `it is an undertaking`)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
